{"id": "EUVD-2026-98652", "enisaUuid": "3f7f2aea-92a4-3733-9403-82c72e9c4f37", "description": "FreeRDP from 3.0.0 before 3.32.0 contains an uninitialized memory disclosure vulnerability in smartcard_Transmit_Call that allows malicious RDP servers to read client memory. Servers can send SCardTransmit requests with an invalid card handle and nonzero receive length, causing smartcard_pack_transmit_return to serialize up to 66,560 uninitialized heap bytes.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T13:27:15", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T14:06:41", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-f554-v4xw-5j39", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-3.0.0-before-3.32.0-memory-disclosure-via-scardtransmit-smartcard-redirection"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109948", "GHSA-xh9q-86wg-w2r5"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "986f6a7c-6f76-3551-955a-c92313a4bf3d", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "3.0.0 <3.32.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f926f29f-3f72-35ee-ba91-a94ca7c60fcb", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}], "isExploited": false}